      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Although both stress myocardial perfusion imaging and echocardiography may have significant prognostic value, the annual death/myocardial infarction rate appears to be much higher in patients with a negative stress echocardiogram. This may greatly limit its ability to act as a \"gatekeeper\" for additional invasive and interventional procedures."},
